# Line-ending policy for a fleet that must stay byte-identical.
#
# Windows git defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. The live presets under ~/.dsh are LF, so without this file every
# machine would show perpetual phantom changes and rewrite the preset on every
# sync -- a difference that never converges.
#
# Force LF everywhere. These files are configuration, not source with
# platform-specific build expectations.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# never touch binaries
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary

# The journal is an append-only log written from several machines at once. A normal three-way merge
# turns two simultaneous appends into a conflict, and the tempting resolution -- picking a side --
# silently deletes the other session's memory. That is exactly the failure recorded as P44 on the
# remote branch ("two sessions can rewrite the same file inside the same minute").
#
# `union` is git's built-in merge driver for append-only text: both sides' additions are kept. Correct
# for a log, wrong for code, so it is scoped to the journal and to nothing else.
journal/*.md merge=union
